# Git branching and commits

Applies to all projects:

- Commit (and push) directly on `master`/`main` by default; most of these repos have that tendency
- Do **not** create a feature branch unless the user explicitly asks for one
- If a feature branch is created, it must use the prefix `ashaidullin/<branch_name>`
  - Example: `ashaidullin/filter-md-by-fg-input-type`
- Commit messages must be short and descriptive (focus on why, one line preferred)

# C++ builds

Never build or run C++ project tests on the host. Always use the Alma development container:

- Prefer an already-running container named `alma`
- Host path `~/projects` is mounted at `/workspace` inside the container
- Use `docker exec` (not host `ninja`/`cmake`/`g++`)

Example:

```bash
docker exec -u developer -w /workspace/<path-under-projects> alma \
  bash --noprofile --norc -lc '
export PATH="/usr/local/bin:/opt/rh/gcc-toolset-14/root/usr/bin:$PATH"
ninja -C build/so-debug <target>
./build/so-debug/bin/<test-binary>
'
```

If `alma` is not running, start it with the usual `docker run ... --name alma ... platform-alma-8.10-host-uid:latest` workflow before building.
